{
  "format": "lumenet-project",
  "version": 5,
  "universes": 1,
  "notes": "<div><font size=\"5\"><b>Concert</b></font></div><div>A band on a stage of sixteen squares: two moving heads, four RGBW pars at the front, four RGB pars at the back, an LED bar, two blinders, a hazer and the house light. It uses all of it together: lights with their colors, groups, memories with looks and sequences, and a stack that mixes memories, groups, lights and a channel.</div><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">What is in it</font></b></div><ul><li>Groups: Heads, Front, Back, Washes (front and back) and Blinders.</li><li>Memories 1 to 8: the looks of the songs: intro, verse, chorus, bridge, two positions of the heads, the blinders and haze.</li><li>Memories 9 to 13: sequences: a color chase of the back (light steps), the heads swinging, a rainbow of the LED bar, a strobe of the blinders that runs once, a random sparkle.</li><li>The stack: the set, from walk-in to the house light. Steps 4.5 and 9.0 go on by themselves.</li><li>The independents: the blinders, haze, the house light, and the sequences at hand.</li></ul><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">Try it</font></b></div><ol><li>Press <b>Stack</b> and <b>Play</b> through the set. Watch <b>Stage</b> and <b>Fixtures</b> at the same time on another device: <b>LAN</b> lets a phone in.</li><li>During a song, add the back chase (memory 9) or the sparkle (13) with their independent keys; <b>Rate</b> sets the speed of every sequence at once.</li><li><b>Solo up</b> with a key held: only that, at full. <b>Solo down</b>: everything but that.</li><li><b>Fixtures</b> plays any light or group by hand on top: a front par in another color, the heads to a new position.</li><li>Change the set while the stack is off: the <b>Stack</b> view takes memories, channels, lights and groups as steps.</li></ol>",
